irements, but their simultaneous satisfaction is not demonstrated. The lower confidence reflects unresolved flux and fluid chemistry, not the number of steps or environmental ordering.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\",\n        \"rxn_004\",\n        \"rxn_007\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Measure intermediate flux through rxn_003 and rxn_004 under compatible, explicitly defined conditions.\",\n        \"Provide the fluid-composition and buffering balance for the acidic-to-alkaline handoff.\",\n        \"Test the complete processing history without assuming purification between stages.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P8\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.91,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.8,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.79,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.86,\n        \"rxn_008\": 0.98\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.79,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.69,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.76,\n      \"feedback\": \"This history is chemically recognizable and contains no incorrect carbon-skeleton transformation. Confidence is limited by unresolved cyanohydrin-to-aminonitrile flux, unspecified alkaline hydration kinetics, and unquantified acid demand during the hydrolysis handoff. Carryover cyanide, ammonia and buffering species can affect the receiving fluid's composition and should not be omitted from an environmental implementation merely because they cancel from simplified net equations.\",\n      \"approved\": false,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_003\",\n        \"rxn_005\",\n        \"rxn_006\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Characterize the reaction mixture entering the acidic stage, including remaining cyanide, ammonia and alkalinity.\",\n        \"Demonstrate that acidification gives the required pH while retaining the organic intermediate